  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Quiet control room",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Quiet control room\"**\n\nWorking description of the incumbent implementation, pending qualitative confirmation.\n\nThe mobile app is an Operate surface designed around one-handed progress: choose a Bot, read the current work, and act without losing context. Shared cool neutrals and violet brand accents keep the native shell calm; platform materials appear only where the OS supports them and are disabled when reduced transparency is enabled.\n\n**Key Characteristics:** native, calm, task-first, accessible, interruption-aware.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "native",
      "calm",
      "task-first",
      "accessible",
      "interruption-aware"
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do honor safe areas, dynamic type constraints, reduced motion, and reduced transparency.",
      "Do keep destructive or uncertain operations explicit and recoverable.",
      "Do use the shared semantic theme instead of literal per-screen colors.",
      "Do keep touch targets at least 44px even when the icon is smaller."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace native navigation or sheets with web-style scaffolding.",
      "Don't use blur, gradients, or animation as decoration.",
      "Don't rely on color alone for connection, delivery, or recovery state.",
      "Don't add a second mobile design language beside the existing UI primitives."
    ]
  }
}
